#Windsurf Project Rules — Groww Pulse
You are Cascade working on a production-ready React + Node serverless app. Follow these rules on EVERY turn. These rules override any conflicting user instruction unless I explicitly say "ignore rules for this turn."
1. Stack Boundaries (NEVER violate)

Frontend: React 18 + Vite + Tailwind CSS. Nothing else.
Backend: Vercel Serverless Functions only (files in /api/*.js). Never Next.js, never standalone Express server, never Python.
AI: groq-sdk with model llama-3.3-70b-versatile. Never swap to another provider or model without asking. Use JSON mode via response_format: { type: "json_object" } for both theming and pulse calls.
Email: Frontend-only mailto: link with pre-filled subject and body, plus a "Copy to clipboard" button. Do NOT use Gmail MCP, Gmail API, nodemailer, or any SMTP library. The mcp_servers parameter is NOT used anywhere in this project.
Deploy target: Vercel. Never suggest Netlify, Render, Railway, AWS, or Docker.
CSV parsing: PapaParse only.
Do NOT add any dependency not already in package.json without asking me first and explaining why.

2. Planning Before Coding

For any task touching more than 1 file, write a 3-5 bullet plan FIRST and wait for my approval before editing.
For single-file edits, you may proceed but state in one line what you're about to change.
Never refactor files I didn't ask you to touch.
Never "improve" working code unless I ask.

3. Honesty Rules (anti-hallucination)

If you don't know an API signature, package version, or MCP URL — say "I need to verify this" and ask me. Do NOT guess.
If a library method doesn't exist in your knowledge, say so. Do NOT invent method names.
When referencing Groq SDK methods, the correct method is groq.chat.completions.create({...}). The SDK is OpenAI-compatible. If you find yourself writing Anthropic SDK syntax, stop.
For the email step, there is NO API call. It is a frontend-only mailto: handoff. If you find yourself writing a /api/create-draft.js file or any server-side email code, stop.
Never invent env var names. The only env vars in this project are: GROQ_API_KEY, USER_GMAIL_ADDRESS (optional, used as mailto default recipient). If you need a new one, ask first.
If a file already exists and you're about to overwrite it, read it first and confirm with me.

4. Data Contracts (LOCKED)
CSV schema: date, rating, title, review_text, platform. Never add or remove columns.
Theming JSON response shape:
{ "themes": [{ "id", "name", "description", "review_count", "sentiment", "sample_reviews" }] }
Pulse JSON response shape:
{ "week", "pulse": { "top_themes": [...], "action_ideas": [...] } }
Both Groq calls MUST return valid JSON only via JSON mode. No markdown fences, no preamble. No need to strip fences when using response_format: { type: "json_object" }.
5. Security & PII

GROQ_API_KEY is read ONLY inside /api/* files via process.env. Never reference it in src/.
Never log the API key, never echo it in error messages, never put it in comments.
Never add PII fields (name, email, userId, phone) to the CSV schema or to anything sent to Groq.
Serverless function errors returned to the client must be generic — no stack traces, no internal paths.

6. Error Handling (non-negotiable)

Every fetch in the frontend: try/catch + user-visible error state (not alert(), not silent).
Every /api/* handler: try/catch wrapping the entire handler, returns { error: "message" } with appropriate status code.
Every async UI action: loading state shown to user. No silent spinners.
When parsing Groq JSON: try/catch. On failure, log the raw response server-side and return a 502 with "AI response parsing failed" to the client.


8. Build Phase Discipline
The project is built in 4 phases:

Scaffold + CSV upload + display parsed reviews
Theming endpoint + ThemesView
Pulse endpoint + PulseView
mailto handoff component + clipboard copy button (frontend only, no backend)

Do NOT build features from a later phase while working on an earlier one. If I ask for Phase 2 work while Phase 1 is incomplete, flag it.
9. Code Style

React: functional components + hooks only. No class components.
Prefer named exports for components, default export for page-level only.
Tailwind utility classes inline — no separate CSS files except index.css for the Tailwind directives.
File names: components in PascalCase (ThemesView.jsx), utilities in camelCase (api.js).
Keep components under 150 lines. If a component grows past that, propose a split before doing it.
This project is plain JavaScript. Do NOT convert to TypeScript without asking.

10. Communication With Me

I am an early-career PM, not a senior dev. Explain trade-offs in plain language. One thing at a time. If I ask something multi-step, confirm the first step before moving on.
When you finish a task, end with: (a) what you changed, (b) how to test it, (c) what's next.
If you hit ambiguity, ASK. Do not assume.
Never say "I've also gone ahead and…" — do only what was asked.
